                        "entry_id": "b36aee6c-5db0-3ad0-a701-343ce039ae5c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A worker stationed at the South Pole."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "dad07e15-9ca2-4079-a461-757a4dd0efad",
                                "sense_id": "6827b5d9-2a17-31da-aa8c-547d1360cf5b",
                                "text": "Polies have much more attitude than McMurdoites. […] Where a McMurdoite would simply turn and leave a conversation that didn't interest him, a Polie would blatantly change the subject or challenge the entire premise of the discussion."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4150cab0-7e0b-4749-b326-fd5fec665303",
                                "sense_id": "6827b5d9-2a17-31da-aa8c-547d1360cf5b",
                                "text": "“When Polies see the red coats come off the plane, we think they're not real Antarctic workers. We see McMurdo as a luxury resort. We think we're tougher and want the people from McMurdo to see how cold it is and how much ice we have […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "af62c438-ee19-46fe-a5a5-b4654a2663ca",
                                "sense_id": "6827b5d9-2a17-31da-aa8c-547d1360cf5b",
                                "text": "[…] there have been many attempts to do biological and psychological studies on wintering Polies, to see how a genuine Moon base might play out, or one on Mars."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
